cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: >-
  Voblint: A Verified Goblint-Style Static Analysis Pipeline in
  Isabelle/HOL
type: software
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-15"
license: BSD-3-Clause
authors:
  - family-names: Lerchner
    given-names: Manuel
repository-code: >-
  https://github.com/ManuelLerchner/Voblint-Verification-Master-Thesis
url: >-
  https://manuellerchner.github.io/Voblint-Verification-Master-Thesis/
abstract: >-
  Voblint is a machine-checked Isabelle/HOL framework for building, running
  and verifying interprocedural abstract interpreters, modelled on Goblint's
  D/G architecture. It chains verified compilation of a small imperative
  language to a procedure-aware control-flow graph, an activation-local
  operational semantics, executable equation generation, and a vendored
  verified side-effecting top-down solver into one soundness statement about
  the analyzer's own output. The statement covers every configuration the
  tool offers -- five abstract domains, four global update rules, and
  context-insensitive, entry-state and call-string context policies -- and is
  stated about the same operation that is exported to OCaml and runs in the
  command-line tool and the browser playground. Solver termination is a
  per-program premise; lexing, parsing, code generation and rendering lie
  outside the proved chain.
keywords:
  - abstract interpretation
  - static analysis
  - formal verification
  - Isabelle/HOL
  - interprocedural analysis
  - context sensitivity
  - Goblint
  - code generation
